  "body": "`cookieStore.delete(options)` accepts `CookieStoreSetOptions`. It occurs to me that some folks might like to use the `CookieListItem` result of `cookieStore.getAll()` and pass it directly to `delete`, e.g.:\r\n\r\n```js\r\ncookieStore.getAll().then(cookies => Promise.all(map(cookie => cookieStore.delete(cookie))));\r\n```\r\n\r\nPerhaps [`deleteAll`](https://github.com/WICG/cookie-store/issues/58) would satisfy that use case, but maybe I'd want to write an arbitrary filter selecting cookies to delete:\r\n\r\n```js\r\ncookieStore.getAll().then(\r\n  cookies => Promise.all(\r\n    cookies.filter(cookie => cookie.name.length > 6)\r\n    .map(cookie => cookieStore.delete(cookie))\r\n  )\r\n);\r\n```\r\n\r\nIt seems like code like this _could_ work. `CookieListItem` (the result of `getAll`) has a subset of the properties of `CookieStoreSetOptions`. Will it work? Should it work?",
